Usage:
  splitch api-keys create [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>              [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>      [type: string; default: SPLITCH_ENV or config] Environment ID or slug.
  --body-json <json>       [type: JSON object; default: none] Control-plane request fields.
  --idempotency-key <key>  [type: string; default: generated] Stable retry key for this mutation.
  --json                   [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help               [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Credential semantics:
  API Key is secret and server-side only; a newly created value is shown once and cannot be read back.

Example:
  splitch api-keys create --body-json '<json>' --json",
