Commands:
  export          Export an Organization's data.

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch organization-privacy export --help",
    "organization-usage": "Manage organization-usage resources.

Usage:
  splitch organization-usage <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  get             Get an Organization's current-month Evaluation usage breakdown.

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch organization-usage get --help",
    "orgs": "Manage orgs resources.

Usage:
  splitch orgs <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  list            List organizations the token can reach (agent cold-start entry).
  create          Create an organization; the calling principal becomes its owner.
  get             Get one organization.
  update          Rename an organization or change its plan.
  delete          Delete an organization (requires a prior dry-run confirmation token).

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch orgs list --help",
    "privacy-requests": "Manage privacy-requests resources.

Usage:
  splitch privacy-requests <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  get             Get a privacy request's status (and its job, if any).

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch privacy-requests get --help",
    "runs": "Manage runs resources.

Usage:
  splitch runs <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  list            List an Experiment's Runs (newest first).
  get             Get a full Run (frozen assignment + measurement config + status).
  end             End a running Run.

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch runs list --help",
    "segments": "Manage segments resources.

Usage:
  splitch segments <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  list            List Segments in an App.
  create          Create a Segment.
  get             Get a Segment.
  update          Update a Segment.
  delete          Delete a Segment (blocked if referenced by a running Experiment).

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch segments list --help",
  },
  "meta": {
    "context": "Show the logged-in principal and the resolved App and Environment.

Usage:
  splitch context [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>          [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>  [type: string; default: SPLITCH_ENV or config] Environment ID or slug.
  --json               [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help           [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch context --json",
    "health": "Check the Control Plane API health endpoint.

Usage:
  splitch health [flags]

Flags:
  --endpoint <url>  [type: URL; default: resolved platform target origin] Control Plane API base URL.
  --json            [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help        [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch health --endpoint https://api.splitch.dev --json",
    "login": "Authenticate the control-plane session with the browser device flow.

Usage:
  splitch login [--app <app>] [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>  [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --json       [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help   [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch login",
    "logout": "Remove the stored control-plane session.

Usage:
  splitch logout [flags]

Flags:
  --json      [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch logout --json",
    "use": "Select the default App and Environment for the current directory.

Usage:
  splitch use [--app <app>] [--env <environment>] [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>          [type: string; default: unchanged] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>  [type: string; default: unchanged] Environment ID or slug.
  --json               [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help           [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch use --app checkout --env dev --json",
  },
  "root": "splitch - agent-readable feature flag and experimentation control plane

Usage:
  splitch <command> [flags]
  splitch <resource> <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  login           Authenticate the control-plane session with the browser device flow.
  logout          Remove the stored control-plane session.
  use             Select the default App and Environment for the current directory.
  context         Show the logged-in principal and the resolved App and Environment.
  health          Check the Control Plane API health endpoint.

Resource groups:
  api-keys
  app-attention-rollup
  app-privacy
  approval-request-reviews
  approval-requests
  apps
  audit-log
  client-key
  current-user
  current-user-privacy
  entity-privacy
  env-policy
  envs
  experiment-results
  experiments
  flag-config
  flag-targeting-rules
  flag-variants
  flags
  metrics
  organization-members
  organization-privacy
  organization-usage
  orgs
  privacy-requests
  runs
  segments

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Credential semantics:
  Client Key  Public data-plane key for browsers, mobile apps, and other untrusted clients.
  API Key     Secret data-plane key for trusted servers; a newly created value is shown once.

Example:
  splitch flags list --app checkout --json

Run \`splitch <command> --help\` or \`splitch <resource> <action> --help\` for details.",
}
`;
